Step-By-Step Implementation
STEP 1 – Setup Target VM (Metrics Source)

Install Node Exporter:

sudo apt update -y
wget https://github.com/prometheus/node_exporter/releases/download/v1.6.1/node_exporter-1.6.1.linux-amd64.tar.gz
tar xvf node_exporter-1.6.1.linux-amd64.tar.gz
cd node_exporter-1.6.1.linux-amd64
./node_exporter &


Confirm on browser:
http://<target-vm-ip>:9100/metrics

STEP 2 – Setup Monitoring VM (Prometheus + Alertmanager)
 Install Docker
sudo apt update -y
sudo apt install -y docker.io docker-compose
sudo systemctl enable docker
sudo systemctl start docker

 Create Config Files

Inside ~/monitoring/:

prometheus.yml

alert_rules.yml

alertmanager.yml

ai_anomaly_insights.py

STEP 3 – Configure Prometheus

prometheus.yml

global:
  scrape_interval: 15s

scrape_configs:
  - job_name: 'node_exporter'
    static_configs:
      - targets: ['<target-vm-ip>:9100']

STEP 4 – Add Alert Rules

alert_rules.yml

groups:
- name: node_alerts
  rules:
  - alert: NodeExporterDown
    expr: up{job="node_exporter"} == 0
    for: 1m
    labels:
      severity: critical
    annotations:
      summary: "Node Exporter Down"
      description: "The Node Exporter on {{ $labels.instance }} is down."

STEP 5 – Configure Alertmanager

alertmanager.yml

global:
  resolve_timeout: 5m

route:
  receiver: 'aiops-bot'

receivers:
  - name: 'aiops-bot'
    webhook_configs:
      - url: 'http://localhost:5000/alert'

STEP 6 – Run Prometheus and Alertmanager
docker run -d --name prometheus \
  --network host \
  -v ~/monitoring/prometheus.yml:/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml \
  -v ~/monitoring/alert_rules.yml:/etc/prometheus/alert_rules.yml \
  prom/prometheus

docker run -d --name alertmanager \
  --network host \
  -v ~/monitoring/alertmanager.yml:/etc/alertmanager/alertmanager.yml \
  prom/alertmanager


Verify:

Prometheus → http://<vm-ip>:9090

Alertmanager → http://<vm-ip>:9093

STEP 7 – Create Flask AI Alert Receiver

ai_anomaly_insights.py

from flask import Flask, request, jsonify
import requests, json, datetime

app = Flask(__name__)

SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL = "https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXXX/XXXX/XXXX"

@app.route('/alert', methods=['POST'])
def alert_handler():
    data = request.json
    print("Received Alert:", data)

    message = f" *Prometheus Alert Triggered!* \n\n{json.dumps(data, indent=2)}"
    payload = {"text": message}
    requests.post(SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL, json=payload)
    
    return jsonify({"status": "received"})

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=5000)

STEP 8 – Run Flask Service
sudo fuser -k 5000/tcp
nohup python3 ~/monitoring/ai_anomaly_insights.py > ~/monitoring/ai_alerts.log 2>&1 &
tail -f ~/monitoring/ai_alerts.log


